{"content":[{"c":["DEAF, DEAFNESS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Inability to hear; term used in Scripture to describe both a literal, physical inability and a figurative, spiritual defect. The spiritually deaf were those who either refused to hear the divine message or were rendered incapable because of their lack of spirituality (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.38.13","r":"Ps.38.13","rawR":"Ps.38.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.38.13","value":"Ps.38.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 38:13"},"). The prophet Isaiah forcefully addressed both types of deaf persons (the figurative in ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.42.18","r":"Isa.42.18","rawR":"Isa.42.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.42.18","value":"Isa.42.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 42:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.43.8","r":"Isa.43.8","rawR":"Isa.43.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.43.8","value":"Isa.43.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:8"},"; the literal in ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.29.18","r":"Isa.29.18","rawR":"Isa.29.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.29.18","value":"Isa.29.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 29:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.35.5","r":"Isa.35.5","rawR":"Isa.35.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.35.5","value":"Isa.35.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"35:5"},"). In the OT, although the condition was considered the result of God’s judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.4.11","r":"Exod.4.11","rawR":"Exod.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.4.11","value":"Exod.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 4:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.7.16","r":"Mic.7.16","rawR":"Mic.7.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.7.16","value":"Mic.7.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 7:16"},"), it was wrong to curse a deaf person (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.19.14","r":"Lev.19.14","rawR":"Lev.19.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.19.14","value":"Lev.19.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 19:14"},"). In the NT the deaf were among those Jesus healed (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.11.5","r":"Matt.11.5","rawR":"Matt.11.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.11.5","value":"Matt.11.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 11:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.7.32-37","r":"Mark.7.32-37","rawR":"Mark.7.32-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.7.32-37","value":"Mark.7.32-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 7:32-37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.22","r":"Luke.7.22","rawR":"Luke.7.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.22","value":"Luke.7.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 7:22"},"). An epileptic boy whom Jesus healed was afflicted with a “dumb and deaf spirit” (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.9.25","r":"Mark.9.25","rawR":"Mark.9.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.9.25","value":"Mark.9.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 9:25"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Such healings authenticated Jesus’ role as Messiah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"DeafDeafness","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ps 38:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.38.13","rawQueryValue":"Ps.38.13","sourceRefExact":"Ps.38.13"},{"anchorText":"Is 42:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.42.18","rawQueryValue":"Isa.42.18","sourceRefExact":"Isa.42.18"},{"anchorText":"43:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.43.8","rawQueryValue":"Isa.43.8","sourceRefExact":"Isa.43.8"},{"anchorText":"Is 29:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.29.18","rawQueryValue":"Isa.29.18","sourceRefExact":"Isa.29.18"},{"anchorText":"35:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.35.5","rawQueryValue":"Isa.35.5","sourceRefExact":"Isa.35.5"},{"anchorText":"Ex 4:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.4.11","rawQueryValue":"Exod.4.11","sourceRefExact":"Exod.4.11"},{"anchorText":"Mi 7:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.7.16","rawQueryValue":"Mic.7.16","sourceRefExact":"Mic.7.16"},{"anchorText":"Lv 19:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.19.14","rawQueryValue":"Lev.19.14","sourceRefExact":"Lev.19.14"},{"anchorText":"Mt 11:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.11.5","rawQueryValue":"Matt.11.5","sourceRefExact":"Matt.11.5"},{"anchorText":"Mk 7:32-37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.7.32-37","rawQueryValue":"Mark.7.32-37","sourceRefExact":"Mark.7.32-37"},{"anchorText":"Lk 7:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.7.22","rawQueryValue":"Luke.7.22","sourceRefExact":"Luke.7.22"},{"anchorText":"Mk 9:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.9.25","rawQueryValue":"Mark.9.25","sourceRefExact":"Mark.9.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5ca9994bcaf09bcf02f5ee4596947864dcf35b838761a7bbd9e61a480dd11948","sourceItemName":"DeafDeafness","sourceItemOrder":49,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"DeafDeafness","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Deaf, Deafness","title":"Deaf, Deafness","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}